  "Question": "Tangents \\(PA\\) and \\(PB\\) are drawn from a point \\(P\\) outside a circle. If \\(PA=6\\), how long is \\(PB\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "6",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Tangent length theorem: The lengths of the 2 tangent segments drawn to a circle from an external point are equal, so \\(PB=PA=6\\).",
